  "timing_direction": "All 15 pooled request-time and all 15 pooled native-generation comparisons favor K. Cache-maintenance directions are mixed and are retained separately.",
  "fallacy_scan": [
    {
      "name": "Simpson\u2019s paradox",
      "assessment": "Panels and endpoints remain separate; each of the five measured strata favors K in pooled calls and both primary timing measures. No combined-panel claim is used."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ecological fallacy",
      "assessment": "Paired request wins/losses/ties and gross savings/regressions are retained; a positive pooled reduction does not mean every request improved."
    },
    {
      "name": "Berkson\u2019s paradox",
      "assessment": "The fixed eligible task/domain and exclusion recipe limit generalization; the fresh panel is new data from that recipe, not a new model, task family, or training seed."
    },
    {
      "name": "Collider bias",
      "assessment": "No performance-based request filtering is applied. All 320 request-endpoint pairs and all 1,920 executions pass, so no outcome-dependent validity cohort is selected."
    },
    {
      "name": "Base-rate neglect",
      "assessment": "All pooled reductions expose summed O denominators. Per-request percentages are not averaged to obtain the primary result."
    },
    {
      "name": "Regression to the mean",
      "assessment": "Endpoints and panels were fixed before outcomes, with matched O/K comparisons; this does not convert a nonmonotonic curve into a causal training-age effect."
    },
    {
      "name": "Survivorship bias",
      "assessment": "Complete six-slot coverage is present for every request-endpoint. Operational stop/transfer failures are preserved separately; they are not represented as scientific retries or discarded bad endpoints."
    },
    {
      "name": "Look-elsewhere effect",
      "assessment": "All five prespecified event/panel strata and all three timing repeats are shown; no best-repeat or best-panel selection and no significance claim."
    },
    {
      "name": "Garden of forking paths",
      "assessment": "The audit script hash matches its pre-outcome readiness receipt. No denominator, timing aggregation or endpoint rule changed after reading outcomes."
    },
    {
      "name": "Correlation versus causation",
      "assessment": "These are measurements of one controlled continuation. The curve alone does not establish a general training-duration effect or adaptation-inclusive asynchronous speedup."
    },
    {
      "name": "Reverse causality",
      "assessment": "Checkpoint order precedes evaluation and no reverse-direction causal inference is made; observational curve shape is not assigned a mechanism."
    }
  ],
